wasi-libc's LICENSE also names dlmalloc (CC0, which asks for no notice),
emmalloc, and musl-fts. Neither emmalloc, an allocator wasi-libc builds only
when asked to instead of dlmalloc, nor fts, a file-tree walker a reactor with
no file system does not call, is bundled; without a producers section that is
an assumption about the build, not a verified fact.

The binary is not rebuilt from source; a unit test (`src/engine.rs`) checks
the embedded bytes against the SHA-256 above and that this record names it. To
update, replace the file, this record, and `QUICKJS_WASM_SHA256`, then
re-check the driver's ABI (the exports `src/guest.rs` names and their
signatures) and the license files against the new versions.
